Searching

Searching in GitHub is based on Rust

GitHub Code Search

"/" on a GitHub page to automatically start searching

Search Qualifiers

Flex Qualifiers
	Example -> "type" like "user' or "org"
	Example -> "is" like "archived" or "issue"
	Example -> "in" like "title" or "comments"

After starting a search
	Advanced search panel on Left side of screen

Advanced Search

You can save the search and search results for later
	Hit "Save" button at top of search results

Syntax Operators
	Comparisons: >, >=, <, <=
	Ranges: 10..*, *..10, 10..100
		"*" for "some amount"
	Date-Time: YYYY-MM-DD, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
	Excluded: -, NOT
	Quotations: ""

	Example Search:
		"syntax highlighter" NOT images NOT python stars:>100 language:JavaScript pushed:>2026-01-01

Sorting
	sort:*
	-asc, -dsc
	-date, -indexed, -updated

	Example Search:
		"react ui components" stars:>1000 sort:date-asc

When searching for code

"username".githut.io
	Creating a repository with this name becomes the default repository

	alexanderfoster14-glicht.github.io WOULD be the default repository

Example search:
	repo:planetoftheweb/planetoftheweb.github.io language:Markdown path:newsletter morten AND prototype
	pulls up list of files that has "morten' and "prototype" included

"Raw" at top right
	pulls up a page to make it easy to copy/paste just the code

Ellipses on Left "..." in a file
	helpful to copy or see info about who created something

Searching for a file to learn something
	Example search:
	dockerfile language:Dockerfile path:/^.devcontainer\// python org:LinkedInLearning

Symbols panel
	Right panel when looking at a code file
	can find "non-standard" symbols (key terms)













